::UserStylesheet [stylesheet]
/* ============================================================
   DASH DIET GAME — visual stylesheet
   Phone-frame UI, viridis dark gradient (purple-blue-teal-green-yellow),
   large emoji food cards. Sister game to Salt Sludge.

   CardioCareQuest viridis palette (canonical across all games):
     #440154  deep purple   — phone gradient stop 1
     #3b528b  blue          — phone gradient stop 2
     #21918c  teal          — phone gradient stop 3 / meter correct
     #5ec962  green          — selected / verdict good (#0a3d12 deep)
     #fde725  yellow         — primary CTA / attention / in-text links
     #f4f1d8  cream          — page background
   ============================================================ */

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
  background-color: #f4f1d8;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 1.5em 0;
}

#ui-bar { display: none; }

#story {
  margin: 0 auto;
  max-width: 380px;
  padding: 0;
}

.passage {
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1em;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

/* Phone frame — viridis purple-blue gradient */
.phone {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #440154 0%, #3b528b 50%, #21918c 100%);
  border-radius: 32px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
  color: #ffffff;
  position: relative;
  min-height: 660px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
}

.phone *, .phone *::before, .phone *::after {
  word-wrap: break-word;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
  max-width: 100%;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Force ALL paragraphs and divs inside .phone to wrap — defends against any
   SugarCube default styles that might force overflow on text content */
.phone p, .phone div {
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
}

/* Header */
.header {
  padding: 16px 22px;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  font-weight: bold;
  color: #ffffff;
  font-size: 16px;
  background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
  flex: 0 0 auto;
}
.header .round-label {
  opacity: 0.75;
  font-size: 14px;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}

/* Twin meter section — correct (green) and wrong (purple) */
.meters-wrap {
  padding: 10px 22px 6px 22px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
}
.meter-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.meter-label {
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.85;
  width: 72px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.meter-bar {
  flex: 1;
  height: 10px;
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 6px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.meter-bar-fill {
  height: 100%;
  border-radius: 6px;
  transition: width 0.4s ease;
  width: 0%;
}
.meter-bar-fill.correct {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #21918c 0%, #5ec962 100%);
}
.meter-bar-fill.wrong {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #440154 0%, #3b528b 100%);
}

/* Single score bar for meal builder */
.score-bar-wrap {
  padding: 12px 22px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.score-label {
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.85;
  width: 80px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.score-bar {
  flex: 1;
  height: 12px;
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 6px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.score-bar-fill {
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #21918c 0%, #5ec962 100%);
  border-radius: 6px;
  transition: width 0.4s ease;
  width: 0%;
}

/* Content area */
.content {
  padding: 12px 20px 20px 20px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.spacer { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 6px; }

/* Title for narrative screens */
.intro-title {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 32px;
  font-weight: normal;
  margin: 0 0 16px 0;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
}

/* Hero emoji */
.hero-emoji {
  font-size: 90px;
  line-height: 1;
  text-align: center;
  display: block;
  margin: 8px auto 16px auto;
}

/* Narrative body */
.narrative {
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  margin: 0 0 12px 0;
  text-align: left;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  color: #ffffff !important;
}
.narrative.center { text-align: center; }
.narrative:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }

/* Round Start screen */
.round-status {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  margin: 6px 0 14px 0;
  opacity: 0.88;
}

/* Quiz card — single big food in white card */
.quiz-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 28px 22px;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
  min-height: 240px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.quiz-emoji {
  font-size: 90px;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  display: block;
}
.quiz-name {
  font-size: 26px;
  font-weight: bold;
  margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  color: #1a1a1a;
}
.quiz-desc {
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: #555;
  margin: 0;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
  hyphens: auto;
}

.question-prompt {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 14px;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.8;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

/* Quiz choice buttons — green for lowers, purple for raises */
.choice-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 10px;
}
.choice-btn,
.phone a.choice-btn,
.phone a.choice-btn.macro-link,
.phone a.choice-btn.link-internal {
  display: block !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  padding: 16px 14px !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
  font-size: 15px !important;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
  border: 2px solid !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
  min-height: 48px !important;
  display: flex !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
}
.choice-btn.lowers,
.phone a.choice-btn.lowers,
.phone a.choice-btn.lowers.macro-link {
  background-color: #5ec962 !important;
  color: #0a3d12 !important;
  border-color: #5ec962 !important;
}
.choice-btn.raises,
.phone a.choice-btn.raises,
.phone a.choice-btn.raises.macro-link {
  background-color: #440154 !important;
  color: #ffffff !important;
  border-color: #440154 !important;
}

/* Result card on Food Result screen */
.result-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 22px 20px;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
  min-height: 320px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.result-emoji {
  font-size: 70px;
  line-height: 1;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  display: block;
}
.result-verdict {
  font-size: 26px;
  font-weight: bold;
  margin: 0 0 14px 0;
}
.result-verdict.correct { color: #21918c; }
.result-verdict.wrong { color: #440154; }
.result-explain {
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: #444;
  margin: 0;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
  hyphens: auto;
}

/* Meal builder ingredients */
.section-label {
  font-size: 12px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  opacity: 0.85;
  margin: 14px 0 8px 0;
  font-weight: bold;
}
.section-label:first-of-type { margin-top: 4px; }

.ingredients-grid {
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: row !important;
  flex-wrap: wrap !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  justify-content: flex-start !important;
  align-items: stretch !important;
  margin: 0 -5px !important;
}

/* Each ingredient wrapper is the visible card */
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap {
  background-color: #ffffff !important;
  color: #1a1a1a !important;
  border: 2px solid transparent !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  padding: 16px 8px !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: column !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
  min-height: 120px !important;
  width: calc(50% - 10px) !important;
  flex-grow: 0 !important;
  flex-shrink: 0 !important;
  flex-basis: calc(50% - 10px) !important;
  max-width: calc(50% - 10px) !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1) !important;
  margin: 5px !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  transition: all 0.25s ease !important;
}

/* Selected state — added via <<run>> jQuery call when user taps */
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap.selected {
  background-color: #5ec962 !important;
  border-color: #21918c !important;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(33, 145, 140, 0.35) !important;
}
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap.selected .ing-name,
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap .added-name {
  color: #0a3d12 !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
}
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap.selected .ing-emoji {
  filter: brightness(1.1);
}

/* Inner linkreplace span — transparent, fills the wrapper */
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap .macro-linkreplace {
  background-color: transparent !important;
  color: inherit !important;
  border: none !important;
  padding: 0 !important;
  margin: 0 !important;
  box-shadow: none !important;
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: column !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
}
.ingredients-grid .ing-wrap .macro-linkreplace a {
  color: inherit !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  display: flex !important;
  flex-direction: column !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
}

/* Fallback for the .added-name text — readable even without .selected */
.added-name {
  color: #0a3d12 !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
}

.ing-emoji {
  font-size: 50px !important;
  line-height: 1 !important;
  margin-bottom: 8px !important;
  display: block !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
}
.ing-name {
  font-size: 14px !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
  line-height: 1.2 !important;
  color: #1a1a1a !important;
  display: block !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  width: 100% !important;
}

/* Meal result list */
.meal-list-card {
  background-color: #ffffff;
  border-radius: 18px;
  padding: 20px;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.meal-list-card .list-title {
  font-size: 13px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: #888;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  text-align: center;
}
.meal-list-card .meal-emojis {
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 36px;
  line-height: 1.2;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict {
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: center;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
/* Verdict colors map to viridis stops in their natural order:
   strong = teal (mid viridis), moderate = green (75%), mixed =
   warm-amber semantic-warning (off-palette by design — same
   convention Vascular Village uses for BP stage-1), weak = deep
   purple (low end of viridis, "off the bottom of the scale"). */
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.strong { color: #21918c; }
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.moderate { color: #5ec962; }
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.mixed { color: #f0a020; }
.meal-list-card .meal-verdict.weak { color: #440154; }
.meal-list-card .meal-explain {
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: #444;
  margin: 0;
  text-align: left;
  word-wrap: break-word !important;
  overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  white-space: normal !important;
  max-width: 100% !important;
  hyphens: auto;
}

/* Buttons */
.btn-primary,
.phone a.btn-primary,
.phone a.btn-primary.link-internal,
.phone a.btn-primary.macro-link {
  display: block !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  padding: 16px !important;
  background-color: #fde725 !important;
  color: #2a1a4a !important;
  border: none !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  font-weight: bold !important;
  font-size: 16px !important;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  cursor: pointer !important;
  margin-bottom: 10px !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
}
.btn-secondary,
.phone a.btn-secondary,
.phone a.btn-secondary.link-internal,
.phone a.btn-secondary.macro-link {
  display: block !important;
  width: 100% !important;
  padding: 12px !important;
  background-color: transparent !important;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3) !important;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85) !important;
  border-radius: 14px !important;
  font-size: 13px !important;
  letter-spacing: 0.05em !important;
  text-align: center !important;
  text-decoration: none !important;
  font-family: 'Atkinson Hyperlegible', system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif !important;
  box-sizing: border-box !important;
  min-height: 48px !important;
  display: flex !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  justify-content: center !important;
}

/* Plain in-text links */
.phone a.link-internal:not(.btn-primary):not(.btn-secondary):not(.choice-btn):not(.ingredient):not(.macro-link),
.phone a.macro-link:not(.btn-primary):not(.btn-secondary):not(.choice-btn):not(.ingredient) {
  color: #fde725;
}



::UserScript [script]

/* CardioCare Quest — auto passage telemetry.
   Fires `passage_entered` for every passage entry via the FlutterBridge.
   Snapshots SugarCube state.variables so researchers see the player's
   path plus key in-game state. Best-effort; swallows errors. */
$(document).on(":passagestart", function (ev) {
  try {
    if (window.CCQ && typeof window.CCQ.telemetry === "function") {
      var snap = {};
      try { Object.assign(snap, SugarCube.State.variables); } catch (e) {}
      CCQ.telemetry("passage_entered", {
        passage: ev.passage.title,
        vars: snap
      });
    }
  } catch (e) { /* swallow */ }
});


/* DASH Diet Game — Meal Builder ingredient TOGGLE handler.
   Replaces the earlier `<<linkreplace>>` markup which was one-way
   (commit on first tap, no undo). With this handler, every
   `.ing-wrap` is fully toggleable: tap to add → tap again to remove.
   - $meal array is the source of truth for what's been added.
   - $mealScore is recomputed delta-style as items are added/removed.
   - The score bar's width is updated directly (not via SugarCube
     re-render) so the bar moves smoothly inside the same passage.
   - On re-entry to Meal Builder (e.g. via Restart), the handler
     reconstructs the visual state from $meal so previously selected
     items still show as Added.
*/
$(document).on(":passagedisplay", function (ev) {
  if (!ev || !ev.passage || ev.passage.title !== "Meal Builder") return;

  function refreshScoreBar() {
    var fill = document.querySelector(".score-bar-fill");
    if (!fill) return;
    var score = (State.variables && State.variables.mealScore) || 0;
    // Empty-to-full scale, NOT centred around 50%. Sum of all positive
    // ingredient scores is +80 (10+15+15+10+10+10+5+5), so multiply
    // by 1.25 to map a "perfect" meal (+80) to 100% width. Negative
    // ingredients clamp at 0% — bar empties, doesn't drop below.
    // Earlier formula was `score + 50` which painted an empty meal as
    // a half-full bar before the player tapped anything; this is more
    // intuitive ("nothing picked = empty bar").
    var pct = Math.max(0, Math.min(100, score * 1.25));
    fill.style.width = pct + "%";
  }

  function setSelected(wrap, selected) {
    var nameSpan = wrap.querySelector(".ing-name");
    var rawName = wrap.dataset.ingName || "";
    if (selected) {
      wrap.classList.add("selected");
      if (nameSpan) {
        nameSpan.textContent = "✓ Added";
        nameSpan.classList.add("added-name");
      }
    } else {
      wrap.classList.remove("selected");
      if (nameSpan) {
        nameSpan.textContent = rawName;
        nameSpan.classList.remove("added-name");
      }
    }
  }

  var wraps = document.querySelectorAll(".ing-wrap");
  for (var i = 0; i < wraps.length; i++) {
    var wrap = wraps[i];
    if (wrap.dataset.handlerAttached === "yes") continue;
    wrap.dataset.handlerAttached = "yes";

    var name = wrap.dataset.ingName || "";
    var emoji = wrap.dataset.ingEmoji || "";
    var fullLabel = emoji + " " + name;

    // Restore previously-selected state if the player navigated away
    // and back. Without this every Meal Builder revisit would render
    // unselected even though $meal still contains the items.
    var existingMeal = (State.variables && State.variables.meal) || [];
    if (existingMeal.indexOf(fullLabel) !== -1) {
      setSelected(wrap, true);
    }

    wrap.addEventListener("click", (function (wrap, name, emoji, fullLabel) {
      return function () {
        var scoreDelta = parseInt(wrap.dataset.ingScore || "0", 10);
        var meal = (State.variables.meal || []).slice();
        var idx = meal.indexOf(fullLabel);
        if (idx !== -1) {
          // UNSELECT — remove from $meal, undo score, revert visual.
          meal.splice(idx, 1);
          State.variables.mealScore =
              (State.variables.mealScore || 0) - scoreDelta;
          setSelected(wrap, false);
        } else {
          // SELECT — push to $meal, add score, mark as Added.
          meal.push(fullLabel);
          State.variables.mealScore =
              (State.variables.mealScore || 0) + scoreDelta;
          setSelected(wrap, true);
        }
        State.variables.meal = meal;
        refreshScoreBar();
      };
    })(wrap, name, emoji, fullLabel));
  }
});



::DashHelpers [script]
/*
DASH Diet Game — food POOL + weighted, non-repeating picker.
Convention: game logic lives here in a [script] passage's setup.*
namespace rather than inline in passages (mirrors Salt Sludge's
SaltHelpers). UPDATE6 (no repeat), UPDATE7 (self-terminating via
null), UPDATE8 (weight the draw toward packaged foods).

setup.dash.foods — every classifiable food. Each object:
  { id, emoji, name, desc, correct: 'lowers'|'raises', explain, packaged }
The emoji / name / desc / correct / explain content for the first six
items is lifted verbatim from the old hardcoded Food Card 1..6 + the
Food Result explain chain; the remaining packaged items were added so
the packaged-weighting actually biases the draw.
*/
setup.dash = setup.dash || {};

setup.dash.foods = [
  {
    id: "banana",
    emoji: "🍌",
    name: "Banana",
    desc: "A common fruit. Sweet. Easy to find. You probably already know someone who eats one every morning.",
    correct: "lowers",
    explain: "Bananas are high in potassium, which helps your kidneys flush excess sodium out. Less sodium means less pressure on your artery walls. A banana a day is a real cardiovascular tool.",
    packaged: false
  },
  {
    id: "noodles",
    emoji: "🍜",
    name: "Instant Noodles",
    desc: "Quick to make. Inexpensive. A meal that shows up in most kitchens at some point.",
    correct: "raises",
    explain: "One packet of instant noodles can contain 1500 milligrams of sodium. The recommended daily limit is 2300. One packet gets you halfway there before anything else.",
    packaged: true
  },
  {
    id: "darkchocolate",
    emoji: "🍫",
    name: "Dark Chocolate",
    desc: "Not milk chocolate. Dark, seventy percent cacao or higher. A small square. Not a whole bar.",
    correct: "lowers",
    explain: "Dark chocolate contains flavonoids that help blood vessels relax and widen. A small amount, around one square, can produce a measurable drop in blood pressure. The key word is small.",
    packaged: false
  },
  {
    id: "bacon",
    emoji: "🥓",
    name: "Bacon",
    desc: "Cured in salt. High in saturated fat. A food that appears on a lot of breakfast plates.",
    correct: "raises",
    explain: "Bacon is cured in salt and high in saturated fat. Sodium increases blood volume. Saturated fat stiffens artery walls. Together they are a real cardiovascular load.",
    packaged: true
  },
  {
    id: "spinach",
    emoji: "🥬",
    name: "Spinach",
    desc: "A leafy green. Eaten raw or cooked. Shows up in salads, soups, side dishes.",
    correct: "lowers",
    explain: "Spinach is high in potassium and magnesium, two minerals that directly support healthy blood pressure. One of the most nutrient-dense foods for the heart.",
    packaged: false
  },
  {
    id: "cannedsoup",
    emoji: "🥫",
    name: "Canned Soup",
    desc: "Warm. Convenient. A common meal for busy days or cold evenings.",
    correct: "raises",
    explain: "One serving of canned soup often contains 800 to 1200 milligrams of sodium. Many cans hold two servings. Checking labels on canned food is one of the best things you can do for blood pressure.",
    packaged: true
  },
  {
    id: "pretzels",
    emoji: "🥨",
    name: "Salted Pretzels",
    desc: "A crunchy snack straight from the bag. Twisted, golden, coated in coarse salt.",
    correct: "raises",
    explain: "Those salt crystals on top are the giveaway. A single serving of pretzels carries several hundred milligrams of sodium, and the bag rarely holds just one serving.",
    packaged: true
  },
  {
    id: "frozenpizza",
    emoji: "🍕",
    name: "Frozen Pizza",
    desc: "Straight from the freezer to the oven. Cheese, cured toppings, a salted crust.",
    correct: "raises",
    explain: "Between the cheese, the processed meat, and the dough, one frozen pizza can hold most of a day's sodium in a single meal.",
    packaged: true
  },
  {
    id: "deliham",
    emoji: "🍖",
    name: "Deli Ham",
    desc: "Sliced at the deli counter. Pink, thin, ready for a sandwich.",
    correct: "raises",
    explain: "Processed deli meats are cured and preserved with salt. A few slices deliver a surprising sodium load before the bread is even added.",
    packaged: true
  },
  {
    id: "sweetpotato",
    emoji: "🍠",
    name: "Sweet Potato",
    desc: "An orange root vegetable. Baked, roasted, or mashed. Naturally sweet.",
    correct: "lowers",
    explain: "Sweet potato is quietly one of the best blood pressure foods. High in potassium, low in sodium. Your arteries appreciate it.",
    packaged: false
  }
];

/* Draw the next food:
   - candidates = foods not yet in seenFoods (UPDATE6, no repeats)
   - none left  -> return null so Round Start ends the quiz (UPDATE7)
   - otherwise weight packaged items 2.5x vs 1x for fresh (UPDATE8),
     record the pick in seenFoods, stash it in $currentFood, return it. */
setup.dash.pickFood = function () {
  var seen = State.variables.seenFoods || [];
  var candidates = setup.dash.foods.filter(function (f) {
    return seen.indexOf(f.id) === -1;
  });
  if (candidates.length === 0) {
    return null;
  }
  var weights = candidates.map(function (f) {
    return f.packaged ? 2.5 : 1;
  });
  var total = 0;
  for (var i = 0; i < weights.length; i++) {
    total += weights[i];
  }
  var r = Math.random() * total;
  var chosen = candidates[candidates.length - 1];
  for (var j = 0; j < candidates.length; j++) {
    r -= weights[j];
    if (r <= 0) {
      chosen = candidates[j];
      break;
    }
  }
  seen.push(chosen.id);
  State.variables.seenFoods = seen;
  State.variables.currentFood = chosen;
  return chosen;
};


::Story innit [Important/Needed]
/*
SYSTEM CODE: runs once at the very start.

Variables:
- $playerName  : player name
- $score       : total correct quiz answers (0 to 6)
- $wrong       : total wrong quiz answers (0 to 6)
- $mealScore   : meal builder running score
- $round       : current quiz round 1 to 6
- $lastFood    : the food just classified
- $lastCorrect : whether the last answer was right
- $meal        : list of ingredients picked

You do not need to edit this.
*/

<<set $playerName to "Explorer">>
<<set $score to 0>>
<<set $wrong to 0>>
<<set $mealScore to 0>>
<<set $round to 1>>
<<set $lastFood to "">>
<<set $lastCorrect to false>>
<<set $meal to []>>
/* Food-pool state (UPDATE6/7/8): seenFoods tracks which pool ids have
   already been shown this play-through; currentFood is the object the
   generic Food Card / Food Result render. Reset here so PLAY AGAIN
   starts from a full, unshuffled-order pool. */
<<set $seenFoods to []>>
<<set $currentFood to null>>
/* One-shot guard so Meal Result's submitResponse fires exactly once
   per play-through. Reset on Story innit so PLAY AGAIN gets a fresh
   shot. See ::Meal Result for the submit body. */
<<set $submittedThisSession to false>>

<<goto "Welcome">>


::Welcome [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
INCITING MOMENT: Greeting + hook. One button.
Card 1 of 2 before gameplay starts.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🥗</span>

<h1 class="intro-title">DASH Diet Game</h1>

<p class="narrative center">Hey $playerName.</p>

<p class="narrative">DASH means Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension. A way of eating proven to lower blood pressure.</p>

<p class="narrative">This game shows you which everyday foods help and which ones work against you.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="How To Play">HOW IT WORKS</a>

</div>
</div>


::How To Play [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
RULES in one screen.
Card 2 of 2 before gameplay starts.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🍎</span>

<h2 class="intro-title">Two Parts</h2>

<p class="narrative"><strong>Part 1:</strong> Six food cards. Tap whether each food lowers or raises blood pressure. Learn why.</p>

<p class="narrative"><strong>Part 2:</strong> Build a meal. Pick ingredients. See what they do together.</p>

<p class="narrative">Right or wrong, you leave knowing more than you came with.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Round Start">START ROUND 1</a>

</div>
</div>


::Round Start [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
ROUND ROUTER (UPDATE6/7/8).
No longer a UI screen. Draws the next food from the weighted,
non-repeating pool via setup.dash.pickFood(). When the pool is
exhausted pickFood() returns null and we advance to the meal builder
(the same phase the old Food Result advanced to after the last card).
Otherwise we render the single generic Food Card for $currentFood.
*/
<<set _f to setup.dash.pickFood()>>
<<if _f is null>><<goto "Meal Builder Intro">><<else>><<goto "Food Card">><</if>>


::Food Card [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
GENERIC FOOD CARD (UPDATE6/7/8).
Renders whatever setup.dash.pickFood() stashed in $currentFood. The two
choices score against $currentFood.correct: a matching answer bumps
$score and sets $lastCorrect true; a mismatch bumps $wrong and sets it
false. Then on to Food Result. Replaces the old hardcoded Food Card 1..6.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Round $round of <<print setup.dash.foods.length>></span></div>

<div class="meters-wrap">
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Correct</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill correct" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($score / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Wrong</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill wrong" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($wrong / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<div class="quiz-card">
<span class="quiz-emoji"><<print $currentFood.emoji>></span>
<h2 class="quiz-name"><<print $currentFood.name>></h2>
<p class="quiz-desc"><<print $currentFood.desc>></p>
</div>

<div class="question-prompt">What does it do to blood pressure?</div>

<div class="choice-row">

<<link '<span>LOWERS BP</span>'>>
<<set $lastFood to $currentFood.id>>
<<if $currentFood.correct is "lowers">>
<<set $lastCorrect to true>>
<<set $score to $score + 1>>
<<else>>
<<set $lastCorrect to false>>
<<set $wrong to $wrong + 1>>
<</if>>
<<goto "Food Result">>
<</link>>

<<link '<span>RAISES BP</span>'>>
<<set $lastFood to $currentFood.id>>
<<if $currentFood.correct is "raises">>
<<set $lastCorrect to true>>
<<set $score to $score + 1>>
<<else>>
<<set $lastCorrect to false>>
<<set $wrong to $wrong + 1>>
<</if>>
<<goto "Food Result">>
<</link>>

</div>
</div>
</div>

<<script>>
setTimeout(function () {
  var btns = document.querySelectorAll('.choice-row a.macro-link, .choice-row a.link-internal');
  if (btns.length >= 1) btns[0].classList.add('choice-btn', 'lowers');
  if (btns.length >= 2) btns[1].classList.add('choice-btn', 'raises');
}, 0);
<</script>>


::Food Result [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
RESULT OF EACH FOOD CARD.
Tells the player whether they were right and explains why.
Moves to next round or meal builder after round 6.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Round $round of <<print setup.dash.foods.length>></span></div>

<div class="meters-wrap">
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Correct</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill correct" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($score / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
<div class="meter-row"><div class="meter-label">Wrong</div><div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-bar-fill wrong" @style="'width: ' + Math.min(100, ($wrong / 6) * 100) + '%'"></div></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<div class="result-card">
<span class="result-emoji"><<print $currentFood.emoji>></span>

<<if $lastCorrect is true>><div class="result-verdict correct">Correct</div><<else>><div class="result-verdict wrong">Not quite</div><</if>>

<p class="result-explain"><<print $currentFood.explain>></p>
</div>

<!-- Termination is decided by the pool, not by $round: Round Start's
     pickFood() returns null once every food has been seen and routes to
     Meal Builder Intro. So Food Result always just advances the round
     counter and hands back to Round Start for the next draw.
     Per-round "BACK TO CARDIOCAREQUEST" stays removed — the burger
     menu (≡) already exposes "Go to dashboard" on every screen. -->
<<set $round to $round + 1>>
<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Round Start">NEXT FOOD</a>

</div>
</div>


::Meal Builder Intro [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
TRANSITION: Cards done. Introduce meal building.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Part 2</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🍽️</span>

<h2 class="intro-title">Build a Meal</h2>

<p class="narrative center">You scored $score out of <<print setup.dash.foods.length>> on the cards.</p>

<p class="narrative">Now pick ingredients to build a meal. Tap each one to add it. The score bar fills as you choose.</p>

<p class="narrative">No wrong answers here. The point is to see what each choice does.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Meal Builder">START BUILDING</a>

</div>
</div>


::Meal Builder [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
MEAL BUILDER: Player picks ingredients.
Each <<linkreplace>> can be triggered once.
Score bar reflects $mealScore.
*/

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Build a meal</span></div>

<div class="score-bar-wrap">
<span class="score-label">Meal score</span>
<div class="score-bar"><div class="score-bar-fill" @style="'width: ' + Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $mealScore * 1.25)) + '%'"></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<!-- Each ingredient is a plain `<span class="ing-wrap">` with the
     food's emoji / display name / score delta as data-attributes.
     The `:passagedisplay` handler in UserScript wires up TOGGLE
     behaviour on click — earlier this used SugarCube `<<linkreplace>>`
     which is one-way (commits on first tap, no undo) so a player
     who fat-fingered an item couldn't remove it. -->
<div class="section-label">Proteins</div>
<div class="ingredients-grid">
<span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Brown rice" data-ing-emoji="🍚" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍚</span><span class="ing-name">Brown rice</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Beans" data-ing-emoji="🍲" data-ing-score="15"><span class="ing-emoji">🍲</span><span class="ing-name">Beans</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Bacon" data-ing-emoji="🥓" data-ing-score="-15"><span class="ing-emoji">🥓</span><span class="ing-name">Bacon</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Yogurt" data-ing-emoji="🥛" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🥛</span><span class="ing-name">Yogurt</span></span>
</div>

<div class="section-label">Vegetables and Fruit</div>
<div class="ingredients-grid">
<span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Spinach" data-ing-emoji="🥬" data-ing-score="15"><span class="ing-emoji">🥬</span><span class="ing-name">Spinach</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Tomato" data-ing-emoji="🍅" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍅</span><span class="ing-name">Tomato</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Banana" data-ing-emoji="🍌" data-ing-score="10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍌</span><span class="ing-name">Banana</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Potato chips" data-ing-emoji="🍟" data-ing-score="-10"><span class="ing-emoji">🍟</span><span class="ing-name">Potato chips</span></span>
</div>

<div class="section-label">Extras</div>
<div class="ingredients-grid">
<span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Dark chocolate" data-ing-emoji="🍫" data-ing-score="5"><span class="ing-emoji">🍫</span><span class="ing-name">Dark chocolate</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Instant noodles" data-ing-emoji="🍜" data-ing-score="-20"><span class="ing-emoji">🍜</span><span class="ing-name">Instant noodles</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Water" data-ing-emoji="💧" data-ing-score="5"><span class="ing-emoji">💧</span><span class="ing-name">Water</span></span><span class="ing-wrap" data-ing-name="Hot dog" data-ing-emoji="🌭" data-ing-score="-15"><span class="ing-emoji">🌭</span><span class="ing-name">Hot dog</span></span>
</div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Meal Result">SEE MY MEAL RESULT</a>

</div>
</div>


::Meal Result [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
MEAL RESULT: Shows what meal does to BP.
Personalized message based on $mealScore.
Lists what player picked.

The <<run>> below fires the canonical SUBMIT_RESPONSE event so
research data sees a DASH Diet play landing in
`surveys/dash_diet_game/responses/{auto}` and a
`survey_response_submitted` event with surveyId='dash_diet_game'.
The Community Stats engagement-bar query keys on the surveyId,
so without this firing the Diet category bar would stay at 0
no matter how many participants finish the game. Guarded by a
session flag so PLAY AGAIN doesn't double-credit.
*/

<<if not $submittedThisSession>>
<<set $submittedThisSession to true>>
<<run
  try {
    if (window.CCQ && typeof window.CCQ.submitResponse === "function") {
      var verdict = "weak";
      if (State.variables.mealScore >= 30) { verdict = "strong"; }
      else if (State.variables.mealScore >= 10) { verdict = "moderate"; }
      else if (State.variables.mealScore >= 0) { verdict = "mixed"; }
      window.CCQ.submitResponse({
        playerName: State.variables.playerName,
        quizScore: State.variables.score,
        quizWrong: State.variables.wrong,
        mealScore: State.variables.mealScore,
        meal: State.variables.meal,
        verdict: verdict
      }, { pointsEarned: 50, countAsCompletion: true });
    }
  } catch (e) { /* swallow */ }
>>
<!-- UPDATE12: chain the control Daily Check-In off the END of this game.
     Inside the same submit-once guard so it launches exactly once per
     play-through (PLAY AGAIN resets $submittedThisSession in Story innit). -->
<<run try { if (window.CCQ && window.CCQ.launchGame) window.CCQ.launchGame("control_daily_checkin"); } catch (e) {} >>
<</if>>

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span><span class="round-label">Your meal</span></div>

<div class="score-bar-wrap">
<span class="score-label">Meal score</span>
<div class="score-bar"><div class="score-bar-fill" @style="'width: ' + Math.max(0, Math.min(100, $mealScore * 1.25)) + '%'"></div></div>
</div>

<div class="content">

<div class="meal-list-card">
<<if $meal.length gt 0>><div class="meal-emojis"><<for _item range $meal>><<print _item.split(" ")[0]>> <</for>></div><</if>>

<<if $mealScore gte 30>>
<div class="meal-verdict strong">Strong DASH meal</div>
<p class="meal-explain">Your ingredient choices are high in potassium, fiber, and minerals that actively support lower blood pressure. A meal like this, eaten regularly, produces measurable results over weeks.</p>
<<elseif $mealScore gte 10>>
<div class="meal-verdict moderate">Moderate DASH meal</div>
<p class="meal-explain">Some strong choices in there. Swapping one high-sodium ingredient for a potassium-rich one would shift this meal a lot in the right direction.</p>
<<elseif $mealScore gte 0>>
<div class="meal-verdict mixed">Mixed meal</div>
<p class="meal-explain">The DASH-friendly choices are being offset by the high-sodium ones. Small swaps make a real difference here.</p>
<<else>>
<div class="meal-verdict weak">Working against you</div>
<p class="meal-explain">This meal is working against your blood pressure. The sodium load is high and the potassium is low. Try replacing one ingredient and see what changes.</p>
<</if>>
</div>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<a class="btn-primary" data-passage="Story innit">PLAY AGAIN</a>
<!-- Direct goHome via the ccq-home-trigger class — the bridge
     intercepts the click and fires CCQ.goHome() without trampolining
     through the (now unused) Central Hub passage. -->
<a class="btn-secondary ccq-home-trigger" href="javascript:void(0)">BACK TO CARDIOCAREQUEST</a>

</div>
</div>


::Central Hub [Important/Needed nobr]
/*
EXIT HATCH. Hit when the player taps "BACK TO CARDIOCAREQUEST" on
either the Final Result or Meal Result screens. Fires CCQ.goHome() so
the Flutter host pops the WebView route back to the dashboard.
Previously had a "PLAY DASH GAME AGAIN" button that just looped back
to Story innit, leaving participants no way to exit.
*/
<<run
  try {
    if (window.CCQ && typeof window.CCQ.goHome === "function") {
      window.CCQ.goHome();
    }
  } catch (e) { /* swallow */ }
>>

<div class="phone">
<div class="header"><span>DASH Game</span></div>
<div class="content">

<span class="hero-emoji">🏠</span>

<h2 class="intro-title">Returning</h2>

<p class="narrative center">Going back to CardioCareQuest.</p>

<div class="spacer"></div>

</div>
</div>
